      "content": "I'll read both the original test and the CUT source to understand the code before improving it.The original test has a focused test method (`test_from_TemporalAccessor_noDerive`) but is cluttered with ~50 unnecessary imports, 3 unused constants, and the unrelated helper test methods all from a larger test class. I'll produce a clean version that keeps the same methods but strips all dead imports and unused fields.The improved test compiled successfully. The changes made were: removed ~50 unused imports (all ChronoField/Month static imports, serialization, and testing utility imports), removed three unused class-level constants (`MAX_LENGTH`, `TEST`, `PARIS`), and added a brief comment to `test_from_TemporalAccessor_noDerive` explaining why `DateTimeException` is expected — all while preserving identical runtime behaviour across all three test methods."
